58 people died that night in a mass  shooting at the Route 91 Harvest Music  Festival right in front of Mandalay Bay  the death toll would eventually rise to  60. this year marks five years since the  tragedy and this morning we're hearing  from a woman who found her path to  Healing by leaving Las Vegas this is  Joanna hendricks's Survival Story  I remember saying like all I want is  peace in the Years following the Route  91 tragedy Anna Hendricks says she did  everything she could to regain a sense  of normalcy she went to therapy she went  to concerts she helped honor the lives  lost but Las Vegas which was home just  didn't feel the same I think there's an  underlying feeling that's always there  in the city and for her and her three  boys that meant it was time to move on  even to this day I love Vegas but  um Tennessee's healthy for us  Tennessee's a is a place that I have  been able to heal it gets healthy for  them to see me healing when it comes to  dealing with trauma there really is no  right or wrong it's what works for you  Jackie Harris is a behavioral health  consultant for the Vegas strong  resiliency Center she's been counseling  survivors since that tragic night on  October 1st with trauma it's not  something we quote get over you learn to  live a full and healthy and happy life  Diana says that life for her family is  in Tennessee it's different out here  it's very different it's healthier my  oldest said I would never leave here  because it's safe his birthday actually  falls on October 1st and Joanna says  this year they can finally celebrate  without the tragedy casting a shadow  this is the first year in five years but  it kind of just gets to be all about him  she says they'll continue their 58  random acts of kindness to honor the  lives lost but this year offers A New  Beginning yes this happened to us yes it  was a moment of our life but it doesn't  have to stop you  we also want to remind everyone that the  Vegas strong resiliency center is open  this week as it is every week to help  anyone who may need to talk you can find  several resources on their website as  well Vegas strongrc.org
 

